<p>Teaching at St Francis Girls Suwerwa is organised into subject departments, each led by experienced staff responsible for curriculum delivery, practical work, and mentorship within their discipline.</p>

<div class="mvv-grid">
  <div class="mvv-card featured">
    <span class="mvv-icon">🔬</span>
    <h3>Sciences</h3>
    <p>Biology, Chemistry, Physics and Agriculture, our largest department, running the school's fully equipped laboratories.</p>
    <div class="values-row"><span class="value-pill">14 Staff</span></div>
  </div>
  <div class="mvv-card">
    <span class="mvv-icon">🗣️</span>
    <h3>Languages</h3>
    <p>English, Kiswahili, French and German, building the communication and literary skills every learner needs.</p>
    <div class="values-row"><span class="value-pill">12 Staff</span></div>
  </div>
  <div class="mvv-card">
    <span class="mvv-icon">➗</span>
    <h3>Mathematics</h3>
    <p>Pure and applied mathematics, developing the analytical and problem-solving foundation behind our KCSE results.</p>
    <div class="values-row"><span class="value-pill">10 Staff</span></div>
  </div>
  <div class="mvv-card">
    <span class="mvv-icon">🌍</span>
    <h3>Humanities</h3>
    <p>History, Geography, Christian Religious Education and Business Studies, shaping informed, values-driven citizens.</p>
    <div class="values-row"><span class="value-pill">10 Staff</span></div>
  </div>
</div>

<h2 class="section-heading">Departmental Excellence</h2>
<p>Each department sets its own termly objectives, tracks subject performance, and works closely with the Deputy Principal (Academic Affairs) to continuously improve teaching quality. See the results of this structure on our <a href="kcse.html">KCSE Results</a> page.</p>
